@startuml watchwolf-update
title "watchwolf update" -- self-update this checkout, then any install's clones

actor User
participant "cli/watchwolf\n(launcher, on the host)" as Launcher
participant "UpdateCommand\n(in the container)" as Update
participant "GitRepository" as Git
participant "origin\n(git remote)" as Origin
participant "DockerFacade" as Docker
participant "ServersManager /\nClientsManager clones" as Clones

User -> Launcher: bash cli/watchwolf update
activate Launcher
Launcher -> Launcher: compute REPO_ROOT (parent of cli/),\nidentity-mount it, set WW_REPO_ROOT
Launcher -> Update: docker run ... -e WW_REPO_ROOT=<repoRoot> watchwolf-cli:local update
activate Update

== this checkout ==

Update -> Update: read WW_REPO_ROOT
alt WW_REPO_ROOT unset or not a git checkout
    Update --> Launcher: "[i] nothing to self-update" (not a failure)
else identity-mounted checkout found
    Update -> Git: currentBranch()
    Git --> Update: <branch>
    Update -> Git: pullFastForwardOnly(<branch>)
    activate Git
    Git -> Origin: git fetch --prune origin <branch>
    Git -> Git: rev-parse HEAD / origin/<branch>\ngit merge-base --is-ancestor (both directions)
    alt HEAD == origin, or origin is an ancestor of HEAD
        Git --> Update: UpToDate
        note right
          local may be AHEAD of an unmoved
          origin (active development) --
          reported as up to date, untouched
        end note
    else HEAD is an ancestor of origin (clean fast-forward)
        Git -> Git: git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>
        Git --> Update: FastForwarded(fromSha, toSha)
    else neither is an ancestor of the other
        Git --> Update: Diverged(localSha, remoteSha)
        note right: never merged, rebased,\nor touched -- reported only
    else fetch or merge failed
        Git --> Update: Failed(reason)
    end
    deactivate Git

    Update -> Update: report outcome to stdout
    note right
      the rebuild below is UNCONDITIONAL --
      not gated on FastForwarded -- the working
      tree can carry local/unpushed edits a
      pull would never see (see AGENTS.md)
    end note
    Update -> Docker: buildImage(<repoRoot>/cli, WW_IMAGE)
    activate Docker
    Docker -> Docker: docker build (classic builder,\nnot BuildKit -- ~1 minute even if unchanged)
    Docker --> Update: image rebuilt
    deactivate Docker
end

== any install's clones ==

Update -> Clones: is <base>/ServersManager (or ClientsManager) a git checkout?
alt installed
    Update -> Git: currentBranch() (the clone's OWN branch, not a stored config)
    Git --> Update: <branch>
    Update -> Git: pullFastForwardOnly(<branch>)
    Git --> Update: UpToDate / FastForwarded / Diverged / Failed
    Update -> Update: report outcome
else not installed
    Update -> Update: "[i] no install found -- nothing there to update"
end

Update --> Launcher: exit code (OK, or ERROR on any hard failure)
deactivate Update
Launcher --> User: (an exit-10 host-action prompt only applies to other commands;\nupdate needs no root)
deactivate Launcher

@enduml
